{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he went not as time after time to meet the serpents.</b> Because it was said to him, ״כי לא נחש ביעקב״ — 'for there is no enchantment in Jacob' — therefore ״ותהי עליו רוח אלהים״ — 'and the spirit of Elohim came upon him.'" "<b>And he set his face toward the wilderness.</b> For there Israel was, in the plains of Moab, and so that he might see them and direct his soul toward them, that the divine speech might come upon him from HaShem, blessed be He. And Rashi, of blessed memory, interpreted 'and he set his face toward the wilderness' according to its Targum — that is, the Targum rendered it: ושוי למדברא דעבדו ביה עגלא אפוהי — 'and he set toward the wilderness wherein they made the calf,' upon its face. But in precisely checked manuscripts it is not so. And according to the Rabbi, of blessed memory, he recalled against them the accusation of the calf, perhaps he might find an opening to curse them. But according to the manuscripts in which this is not written, it is possible to say that here he intended the spirit of impurity, for at first he directed himself toward the way of faith, and when he wanted divine speech to come to him from HaShem, he recalled at the beginning of his offerings ״ויעל בלק ובלעם פר ואיל״ — 'and Balak and Balaam offered a bull and a ram' — and he wanted Balak to assist him, so that Balaam would slaughter to the attribute of mercy and Balak would throw the blood to the attribute of judgment; but afterward he turned from the way of faith and directed himself toward the spirit of impurity that dwells in the wilderness — this is ״וישת אל המדבר פניו״ — and therefore he recalled here ״ויעל פר ואיל״ — 'and he offered a bull and a ram' — and did not recall Balak, for he did not now want his assistance, so as not to invalidate his intention."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:40.984189095Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}